SBND DQM Archiver
=================

Archives online-monitoring metrics from the Redis database (sbnd-db03) into
the PostgreSQL run-conditions database (sbnd_online_prd).

Files
-----
  Archiver.py          the archiver itself (Python 3)
  archive_offline.sh   offline workflow: run DQM over a ROOT file, then archive
  requirements.txt     python dependencies (redis, psycopg2-binary)
  ddl/                 SQL used to create the monitor tables / monitor map

Setup
-----
Python 3 with the redis and psycopg2 packages is required:

    python3 -m pip install --user -r requirements.txt

or use a virtualenv:

    python3 -m venv env
    source env/bin/activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt

Configuration
-------------
All connection parameters live in a JSON config file. The default is

    /home/nfs/sbnddqm/ArchiverConfig.json

and can be overridden with -c/--config. It defines the PostgreSQL connection
(including "metric_config", the monitor-map table), the Redis connection
(including its password) and the log-file location.

How it works
------------
The monitor map (runcon_prd.monitor_map) defines one row per
(group_name, metric, channel_id) with a monitor type and time interval.
For each row the archiver reads the Redis stream

    <group_name>:<channel_id>:<metric>:archiving

groups entries into epoch-aligned windows of time_interval seconds,
aggregates them with the monitor type (MEAN/MEDIAN/MODE/MAX/MIN/LAST) and
inserts one row per window into runcon_prd.<postgres_table>
(CHANNEL_ID, SMPL_TIME, SMPL_VALUE).

Deduplication: each stream has a high-water mark stored in Redis
("<stream>_LatestCompleted" = ID of the last archived entry). Only entries
newer than the mark are ever read, and the mark is advanced only after the
PostgreSQL commit. Re-inserts after a crash are absorbed by
INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING (the tables have a (channel_id, smpl_time)
primary key). Re-running the archiver therefore never duplicates data.

Usage
-----
One-shot pass (archive everything new, then exit; good for cron):

    python3 Archiver.py

Continuous daemon (scan every 60 s, with archiver_heartbeat):

    python3 Archiver.py --daemon -pr 4

Restrict to a subset of streams:

    python3 Archiver.py -gn tpc_channel -mn rms
    python3 Archiver.py -gn PMT -gn CRT_board

Offline / ROOT-file workflow (phase 2):

    ./archive_offline.sh /path/to/data_..._run20046_....root

which sources the DQM spack environment, runs offline_analysis.fcl over the
file (publishing metrics to Redis) and then runs a one-shot archive pass
with --flush so the trailing, partially-filled time window is archived
immediately. Because of the high-water marks, only the metrics generated by
the offline job (plus anything else new in Redis) are archived.

Useful options
--------------
  --flush                also archive the trailing incomplete time window
  --grace S              wait S seconds after a window closes before
                         archiving it (default 60)
  --interval-override S  override the monitor-map time interval; 0 archives
                         every sample without aggregation
  -pr N                  split the streams over N worker processes
  -ch ID                 single channel (debugging)
  --daemon               run forever
  --poll-interval S      seconds between daemon scans (default 60)
